# Copy this file to `secrets.properties` and fill in the values.
#
# `secrets.properties` is gitignored and must never be committed. This template
# is tracked so a clean clone knows what it needs without anyone having to guess
# the key names.
#
# MAPS_API_KEY is a Google Cloud API key with the Maps SDK for Android and the
# Places API enabled. It is embedded in the APK at build time and is therefore
# extractable by anyone who has the app - that is unavoidable for an Android
# Maps key and is why Google's protection model is server-side restriction, not
# secrecy. Before using this key anywhere but a debug build, restrict it in the
# Cloud console to:
#
#   - Application restriction: Android apps
#       package name: com.ss.medrecord
#       SHA-1 of the signing certificate (debug and release are different keys,
#       so add both)
#   - API restriction: Maps SDK for Android, Places API
#
# An unrestricted key found in an APK will be used by someone else, on your
# billing account.
#
# Leaving this blank is safe: the build still succeeds and the map degrades to
# a message saying it is unavailable, rather than crashing.
MAPS_API_KEY=
